  "evidenceId": "2026-09-25-unreachable-budget-accounting",
  "date": "2026-09-25",
  "subject": "Bounded collection of unreachable internal memory-budget owners",
  "claim": "The existing memory-budget accounting fixture passes 54 cases on Windows and Debian after adding 25 collector checks to its prior 29 cases. Collection preserves current-generation live budgets and allocation leases, ignores stale generations, defers parent reclamation while a child lease remains live, returns malformed inputs unchanged, handles empty and duplicate roots, accepts the 2,162,688-byte root ceiling and rejects one extra cell before scanning, and reclaims a full 65-entry table while retaining the highest-index live child. Two source compilations per host produce the same 49,269-byte WVB; each module passes complete verification. Profile-1 native execution returns 42 on both hosts. Debian execution peaks at 11,812,864 bytes of resident memory.",
  "source": {
    "kind": "GitCommit",
    "value": "c1de7f957b3a5fe789d6729119ac846ed2779a7c"
  },
